<div id="A2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">For <span id="A2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">PersonaBench</span>, we adopt the session-level memory construction as in the benchmark paper, which enables fair evaluation of retrieval quality using Recall. We evaluate our method under multiple retrievers, including <span id="A2.p3.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">multi-qa-MiniLM-L6-cos-v1<span id="footnote4" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">4</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">4</sup>
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note"><span id="footnote4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_serif">4</span></span>
              
              
              
            <a href="https://huggingface.co/sentence-transformers/multi-qa-MiniLM-L6-cos-v1" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_url">https://huggingface.co/sentence-transformers/multi-qa-MiniLM-L6-cos-v1</a></span></span></span></span>, <span id="A2.p3.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">all-MiniLM-L6-v2<span id="footnote5" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">5</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">5</sup>
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note"><span id="footnote5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_serif">5</span></span>
              
              
              
            <a href="https://huggingface.co/sentence-transformers/all-MiniLM-L6-v2" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_url">https://huggingface.co/sentence-transformers/all-MiniLM-L6-v2</a></span></span></span></span>, and <span id="A2.p3.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">bge-base-en-v1.5<span id="footnote6" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">6</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">6</sup>
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note"><span id="footnote6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_serif">6</span></span>
              
              
              
            <a href="https://huggingface.co/BAAI/bge-base-en-v1.5" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_url">https://huggingface.co/BAAI/bge-base-en-v1.5</a></span></span></span></span> to ensure generality.
For Recall@5, we use <math id="A2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B=3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B=3</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F=1</annotation></semantics></math>; for Recall@10, we use <math id="A2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B=3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B=3</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F=2</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda=30" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>30</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda=30</annotation></semantics></math> for both. The thresholds are set to <math id="A2.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{\text{high}}=0.6" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mtext>high</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.6</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{\text{high}}=0.6</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{\text{low}}=0.0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mtext>low</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{\text{low}}=0.0</annotation></semantics></math>, reflecting the lower similarity scores in session-level indices. And we illustrate the mean score <math id="A2.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>s</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{s}</annotation></semantics></math> and entropy <math id="A2.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H(p)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H(p)</annotation></semantics></math> of the PersonaMem dataset in Figure <a href="#A2.F8" title="Figure 8 ‣ Appendix B Implementation details ‣ Evoking User Memory: Personalizing LLM via Recollection-Familiarity Adaptive Retrieval" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>. <span id="A2.p3.1.5" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> Also, for support our theorical assumption in Appendix <a href="#A6.SS3" title="F.3 Sub-Gaussian Mean Similarity and Gating Reliability ‣ Appendix F Theoretical Analysis ‣ Evoking User Memory: Personalizing LLM via Recollection-Familiarity Adaptive Retrieval" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">F.3</span></a>, we show the empirical distribution of mean score <math id="A2.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">s</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">¯</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{s}</annotation></semantics></math> in the Figure <a href="#A2.F9" title="Figure 9 ‣ Appendix B Implementation details ‣ Evoking User Memory: Personalizing LLM via Recollection-Familiarity Adaptive Retrieval" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a>.</span></p>
</div>
