<div id="A2.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">For <span id="A2.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">LongMemEval</span>, we also adopt the session-level memory construction as in the paper, with recall as a metric. We also evaluate RF-Mem under <span id="A2.p4.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">multi-qa-MiniLM-L6-cos-v1</span>, <span id="A2.p4.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">all-MiniLM-L6-v2</span>, and <span id="A2.p4.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">bge-base-en-v1.5</span> to ensure generality.
For LongMemEval-S and LongMemEval-M, we use <math id="A2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B=4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B=4</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F=1</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A2.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda=20" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>20</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda=20</annotation></semantics></math>. The thresholds are set to <math id="A2.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{\text{high}}=0.6" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mtext>high</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.6</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{\text{high}}=0.6</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{\text{low}}=0.0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mtext>low</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{\text{low}}=0.0</annotation></semantics></math>. And we illustrate the mean score <math id="A2.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>s</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{s}</annotation></semantics></math> and entropy <math id="A2.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H(p)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H(p)</annotation></semantics></math> of the two datasets in Figure <a href="#A2.F10" title="Figure 10 ‣ Appendix B Implementation details ‣ Evoking User Memory: Personalizing LLM via Recollection-Familiarity Adaptive Retrieval" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a> and Figure <a href="#A2.F12" title="Figure 12 ‣ Appendix B Implementation details ‣ Evoking User Memory: Personalizing LLM via Recollection-Familiarity Adaptive Retrieval" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">12</span></a>. <span id="A2.p4.1.5" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> The empirical distribution of mean score <math id="A2.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">s</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">¯</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{s}</annotation></semantics></math> shown in Figure <a href="#A2.F11" title="Figure 11 ‣ Appendix B Implementation details ‣ Evoking User Memory: Personalizing LLM via Recollection-Familiarity Adaptive Retrieval" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a> and Figure <a href="#A2.F13" title="Figure 13 ‣ Appendix B Implementation details ‣ Evoking User Memory: Personalizing LLM via Recollection-Familiarity Adaptive Retrieval" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">13</span></a> also support our theorical assumption in Appendix <a href="#A6.SS3" title="F.3 Sub-Gaussian Mean Similarity and Gating Reliability ‣ Appendix F Theoretical Analysis ‣ Evoking User Memory: Personalizing LLM via Recollection-Familiarity Adaptive Retrieval" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">F.3</span></a>.</span></p>
