<p id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.4" class="ltx_p">for <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r=0,\dots,R-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r=0,\dots,R-1</annotation></semantics></math>, then returns <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\texttt{Top-}K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">Top-</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\texttt{Top-}K</annotation></semantics></math> from the union <math id="A6.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bigcup_{r=0}^{R}\mathcal{C}^{(r)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mo>⋃</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>R</mi></msubsup><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>r</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bigcup_{r=0}^{R}\mathcal{C}^{(r)}</annotation></semantics></math>.
This matches the method description and notation in the main content.</p>
