<section id="A6.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">F.1 </span>Risk-Minimizing Selection</h3>

<div id="A6.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We formalize the selection in equation <a href="#A6.E11" title="In Preliminaries. ‣ Appendix F Theoretical Analysis ‣ Evoking User Memory: Personalizing LLM via Recollection-Familiarity Adaptive Retrieval" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a> as minimizing a retrieval risk that trades correctness and cost.
Let <math id="A6.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}(\text{mode}\mid q)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext>mode</mtext><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}(\text{mode}\mid q)</annotation></semantics></math> denote the probability of returning an insufficient set for <math id="A6.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math> under a mode <math id="A6.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{mode}\in\{\text{Familiarity},\text{Recollection}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>mode</mtext><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mtext>Familiarity</mtext><mo>,</mo><mtext>Recollection</mtext></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{mode}\in\{\text{Familiarity},\text{Recollection}\}</annotation></semantics></math>, and let <math id="A6.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C(\text{mode})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext>mode</mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C(\text{mode})</annotation></semantics></math> denote the expected computation cost.
For a penalty <math id="A6.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> define</p>
<table id="A6.E13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.E13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}(\text{mode}\mid q)=\mathcal{E}(\text{mode}\mid q)+\beta\,C(\text{mode})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext>mode</mtext><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext>mode</mtext><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext>mode</mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}(\text{mode}\mid q)=\mathcal{E}(\text{mode}\mid q)+\beta\,C(\text{mode}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(13)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="Thmlemma1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlemma1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 1</span></span><span id="Thmlemma1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> (Monotonicity of proxy signals)</span></h6>
<div id="Thmlemma1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmlemma1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Assume the similarity distribution admits a monotone likelihood ratio in <math id="Thmlemma1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> between relevant and nonrelevant items, and that the probe softmax temperature <math id="Thmlemma1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math> is fixed.
Then <math id="Thmlemma1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}(\text{Familiarity}\mid q)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">Familiarity</mtext><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}(\text{Familiarity}\mid q)</annotation></semantics></math> is nonincreasing in <math id="Thmlemma1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>s</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{s}</annotation></semantics></math> and nondecreasing in <math id="Thmlemma1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H(p)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H(p)</annotation></semantics></math>, while <math id="Thmlemma1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C(\text{Familiarity})&lt;C(\text{Recollection})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">Familiarity</mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">Recollection</mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C(\text{Familiarity})&lt;C(\text{Recollection})</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A6.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Proof.</em>
Let <math id="A6.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Y_{i}\in\{0,1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Y_{i}\in\{0,1\}</annotation></semantics></math> for the relevance label of item <math id="A6.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> (1 means relevant).Assume a monotone likelihood ratio for scores so the posterior relevance <math id="A6.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi(s)=\Pr(Y=1\mid s)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi(s)=\Pr(Y=1\mid s)</annotation></semantics></math> is nondecreasing in <math id="A6.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>s</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s</annotation></semantics></math>.
For <span id="A6.SS1.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text">Familiarity</span>, the miss probability given scores is <math id="A6.SS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\prod_{i\in K}\bigl(1-\pi(s_{i})\bigr)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo lspace="0em" maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\prod_{i\in K}\bigl(1-\pi(s_{i})\bigr)</annotation></semantics></math>.
Any coordinatewise increase of <math id="A6.SS1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(s_{i})_{i\in K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(s_{i})_{i\in K}</annotation></semantics></math> decreases each factor, hence decreases the product, so <math id="A6.SS1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}(\text{Familiarity}\mid q)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext>Familiarity</mtext><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}(\text{Familiarity}\mid q)</annotation></semantics></math> is nonincreasing in <math id="A6.SS1.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>s</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{s}</annotation></semantics></math>.
For entropy, softmax <math id="A6.SS1.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math> is Schur–concave: smaller <math id="A6.SS1.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H(p)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H(p)</annotation></semantics></math> implies larger <math id="A6.SS1.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\max}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\max}</annotation></semantics></math> and larger top margins <math id="A6.SS1.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s_{(1)}-s_{(j)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s_{(1)}-s_{(j)}</annotation></semantics></math>, which increase <math id="A6.SS1.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi(s_{(1)})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi(s_{(1)})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A6.SS1.p2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{i\in I_{K}}\pi(s_{i})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>K</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{i\in I_{K}}\pi(s_{i})</annotation></semantics></math>, thus the product and its expectation are nonincreasing; therefore <math id="A6.SS1.p2.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}(\text{Familiarity}\mid q)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext>Familiarity</mtext><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}(\text{Familiarity}\mid q)</annotation></semantics></math> is nondecreasing in <math id="A6.SS1.p2.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H(p)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H(p)</annotation></semantics></math>.
For costs, <math id="A6.SS1.p2.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C(\text{Familiarity})=\Theta(K\,c_{\mathrm{sim}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext>Familiarity</mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>sim</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C(\text{Familiarity})=\Theta(K\,c_{\mathrm{sim}})</annotation></semantics></math>, while <span id="A6.SS1.p2.1.3" class="ltx_text">Recollection</span> performs at least one extra retrieve–cluster–mix round, so <math id="A6.SS1.p2.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C(\text{Recollection})\geq C(\text{Familiarity})+R\,c_{\mathrm{clust}}(B)&gt;C(\text{Familiarity})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext>Recollection</mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext>Familiarity</mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>clust</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext>Familiarity</mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C(\text{Recollection})\geq C(\text{Familiarity})+R\,c_{\mathrm{clust}}(B)&gt;C(\text{Familiarity})</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A6.SS1.p2.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R\geq 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R\geq 1</annotation></semantics></math>.
 <math id="A6.SS1.p2.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\square" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">□</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\square</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 1</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> (Threshold optimality within monotone policies)</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Consider the class <math id="Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pi</annotation></semantics></math> of policies that are monotone in <math id="Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\bar{s},H)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>s</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\bar{s},H)</annotation></semantics></math> in the sense of Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma1" title="Lemma 1 (Monotonicity of proxy signals) ‣ F.1 Risk-Minimizing Selection ‣ Appendix F Theoretical Analysis ‣ Evoking User Memory: Personalizing LLM via Recollection-Familiarity Adaptive Retrieval" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>.
Within <math id="Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Pi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Π</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pi</annotation></semantics></math>, a two-threshold policy of the form equation <a href="#A6.E11" title="In Preliminaries. ‣ Appendix F Theoretical Analysis ‣ Evoking User Memory: Personalizing LLM via Recollection-Familiarity Adaptive Retrieval" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a> minimizes the pointwise risk equation <a href="#A6.E13" title="In F.1 Risk-Minimizing Selection ‣ Appendix F Theoretical Analysis ‣ Evoking User Memory: Personalizing LLM via Recollection-Familiarity Adaptive Retrieval" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">13</span></a>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A6.SS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Proof.</em>
By Lemma <a href="#Thmlemma1" title="Lemma 1 (Monotonicity of proxy signals) ‣ F.1 Risk-Minimizing Selection ‣ Appendix F Theoretical Analysis ‣ Evoking User Memory: Personalizing LLM via Recollection-Familiarity Adaptive Retrieval" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, <math id="A6.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}(\text{Familarity}\mid q)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext>Familarity</mtext><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}(\text{Familarity}\mid q)</annotation></semantics></math> is nonincreasing in <math id="A6.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>s</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{s}</annotation></semantics></math> and nondecreasing in <math id="A6.SS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math>.
Define</p>
<table id="A6.E14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.E14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t:=\mathcal{L}(\text{Recollection}\mid q),\qquad f(\bar{s},H):=\mathcal{L}(\text{Familiarity}\mid q)=\mathcal{E}(\text{Familiarity}\mid q)+\beta\,C(\text{Familiarity})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext>Recollection</mtext><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>s</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext>Familiarity</mtext><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext>Familiarity</mtext><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mtext>Familiarity</mtext><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t:=\mathcal{L}(\text{Recollection}\mid q),\qquad f(\bar{s},H):=\mathcal{L}(\text{Familiarity}\mid q)=\mathcal{E}(\text{Familiarity}\mid q)+\beta\,C(\text{Familiarity}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(14)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS1.p3.2" class="ltx_p">Then the <span id="A6.SS1.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">Familiarity</span>-region is the sublevel set</p>
<table id="A6.E15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.E15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}:=\{(\bar{s},H):f(\bar{s},H)\leq t\}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>s</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>s</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}:=\{(\bar{s},H):f(\bar{s},H)\leq t\},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(15)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS1.p3.3" class="ltx_p">which is a down-set in <math id="A6.SS1.p3.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="(\bar{s}\uparrow,\,H\downarrow)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>s</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo rspace="0em" stretchy="false">↑</mo><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mi>H</mi><mo rspace="0em" stretchy="false">↓</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\bar{s}\uparrow,\,H\downarrow)</annotation></semantics></math> (“south–east orthant”).
Hence the risk-minimizing monotone policy is <math id="A6.SS1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{1}_{\mathcal{D}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mn>𝟏</mn><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{1}_{\mathcal{D}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Introduce axis-aligned thresholds</p>
<table id="A6.E16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.E16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{\mathrm{high}}:=\inf\{\bar{s}:\ \sup_{H}f(\bar{s},H)\leq t\},\qquad\theta_{\mathrm{low}}:=\sup\{\bar{s}:\ \inf_{H}f(\bar{s},H)&gt;t\}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>high</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.1389em">:=</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">inf</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>s</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.500em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">sup</mo><mi>H</mi></munder><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>s</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>low</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.1389em">:=</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">sup</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>s</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.500em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">inf</mo><mi>H</mi></munder><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>s</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{\mathrm{high}}:=\inf\{\bar{s}:\ \sup_{H}f(\bar{s},H)\leq t\},\qquad\theta_{\mathrm{low}}:=\sup\{\bar{s}:\ \inf_{H}f(\bar{s},H)&gt;t\},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(16)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS1.p3.4" class="ltx_p">and, on <math id="A6.SS1.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{s}\in(\theta_{\mathrm{low}},\theta_{\mathrm{high}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>s</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>low</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>high</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{s}\in(\theta_{\mathrm{low}},\theta_{\mathrm{high}})</annotation></semantics></math>,</p>
<table id="A6.E17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.E17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{\star}(\bar{s}):=\inf\{H:\ f(\bar{s},H)\leq t\},\qquad\tau:=\sup_{\bar{s}\in(\theta_{\mathrm{low}},\theta_{\mathrm{high}})}H_{\star}(\bar{s})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>s</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">:=</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">inf</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.778em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>s</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><mi>H</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo rspace="0.1389em">:=</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">sup</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>s</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>low</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>high</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>s</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{\star}(\bar{s}):=\inf\{H:\ f(\bar{s},H)\leq t\},\qquad\tau:=\sup_{\bar{s}\in(\theta_{\mathrm{low}},\theta_{\mathrm{high}})}H_{\star}(\bar{s}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(17)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS1.p3.5" class="ltx_p">Therefore</p>
<table id="A6.E18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.E18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{Familiarity}\ \Longleftrightarrow\ \big(\bar{s}\geq\theta_{\mathrm{high}}\big)\ \ \text{or}\ \ \big(\theta_{\mathrm{low}}&lt;\bar{s}&lt;\theta_{\mathrm{high}}\ \&amp;\ H\leq\tau\big)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext>Familiarity</mtext><mo lspace="0.778em" rspace="0.778em" stretchy="false">⟺</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>s</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>≥</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>high</mi></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mtext>or</mtext><mspace style="width:1em;" width="1em"></mspace><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>low</mi></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>s</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>high</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.722em">&amp;</mo><mi>H</mi></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{Familiarity}\ \Longleftrightarrow\ \big(\bar{s}\geq\theta_{\mathrm{high}}\big)\ \ \text{or}\ \ \big(\theta_{\mathrm{low}}&lt;\bar{s}&lt;\theta_{\mathrm{high}}\ \&amp;\ H\leq\tau\big),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(18)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS1.p3.6" class="ltx_p">and <span id="A6.SS1.p3.6.1" class="ltx_text">Recollection</span> otherwise, which is exactly the two-threshold gate.  <math id="A6.SS1.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\square" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">□</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\square</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A6.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">F.2 </span>An Entropy Certificate for Correctness</h3>

<div id="A6.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="A6.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\max}=\max_{i}p_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\max}=\max_{i}p_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>.
For fixed <math id="A6.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\max}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\max}</annotation></semantics></math>, the maximal entropy occurs when the residual mass is uniform, that is</p>
<table id="A6.E19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.E19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H(p)\leq h_{2}(p_{\max})+(1-p_{\max})\log(K-1)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H(p)\leq h_{2}(p_{\max})+(1-p_{\max})\log(K-1),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(19)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A6.SS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A6.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{2}(x)=-x\log x-(1-x)\log(1-x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{2}(x)=-x\log x-(1-x)\log(1-x)</annotation></semantics></math> is the binary entropy.
Define the inverse certificate</p>
<table id="A6.E20" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A6.E20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{K}(\tau)=\max\{x\in[1/K,1]:h_{2}(x)+(1-x)\log(K-1)\leq\tau\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{K}(\tau)=\max\{x\in[1/K,1]:h_{2}(x)+(1-x)\log(K-1)\leq\tau\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(20)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="Thmlemma2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmlemma2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma 2</span></span><span id="Thmlemma2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> (Entropy certificate)</span></h6>
<div id="Thmlemma2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmlemma2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmlemma2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">If <math id="Thmlemma2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H(p)\leq\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H(p)\leq\tau</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="Thmlemma2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\max}\geq\phi_{K}(\tau)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\max}\geq\phi_{K}(\tau)</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="A6.SS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Proof.</em>
Rearrange equation <a href="#A6.E19" title="In F.2 An Entropy Certificate for Correctness ‣ Appendix F Theoretical Analysis ‣ Evoking User Memory: Personalizing LLM via Recollection-Familiarity Adaptive Retrieval" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">19</span></a> and apply the definition of <math id="A6.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{K}(\tau)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{K}(\tau)</annotation></semantics></math>.
 <math id="A6.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\square" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">□</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\square</annotation></semantics></math></p>
</div>
<div id="Thmproposition1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmproposition1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition 1</span></span><span id="Thmproposition1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> (Bound on familiarity error under low entropy)</span></h6>
<div id="Thmproposition1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmproposition1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmproposition1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Suppose that returning the <math id="Thmproposition1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\texttt{Top-}K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">Top-</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\texttt{Top-}K</annotation></semantics></math> set suffices whenever the true relevant item has <math id="Thmproposition1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{i}\geq\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{i}\geq\rho</annotation></semantics></math> for some <math id="Thmproposition1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math>.
Under <math id="Thmproposition1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H(p)\leq\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H(p)\leq\tau</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="Thmproposition1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{K}(\tau)\geq\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{K}(\tau)\geq\rho</annotation></semantics></math>, the familiarity mode achieves negligible miss probability with respect to this sufficient condition.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A6.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Proposition <a href="#Thmproposition1" title="Proposition 1 (Bound on familiarity error under low entropy) ‣ F.2 An Entropy Certificate for Correctness ‣ Appendix F Theoretical Analysis ‣ Evoking User Memory: Personalizing LLM via Recollection-Familiarity Adaptive Retrieval" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> provides a certificate: a small entropy ensures a large <math id="A6.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{\max}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{\max}</annotation></semantics></math>, which guarantees that the best evidence is included by <math id="A6.SS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\texttt{Top-}K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_monospace">Top-</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\texttt{Top-}K</annotation></semantics></math> under a mild sufficiency condition, hence <span id="A6.SS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">Familiarity</span> is safe in the certified region.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A6.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">F.3 </span>Sub-Gaussian Mean Similarity and Gating Reliability</h3>

<div id="A6.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A6.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Assume probe scores <math id="A6.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{s_{i}\}_{i=1}^{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>s</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{s_{i}\}_{i=1}^{K}</annotation></semantics></math> are independent sub-Gaussian with proxy mean <math id="A6.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math> and variance proxy <math id="A6.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Let <math id="A6.SS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\mu}=\bar{s}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>μ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>s</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\mu}=\bar{s}</annotation></semantics></math> and fix thresholds <math id="A6.SS3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{\text{low}}&lt;\theta_{\text{high}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mtext>low</mtext></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mtext>high</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{\text{low}}&lt;\theta_{\text{high}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmproposition2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmproposition2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition 2</span></span><span id="Thmproposition2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> (Gating error bound via concentration)</span></h6>
<div id="Thmproposition2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmproposition2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmproposition2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For any <math id="Thmproposition2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A6.E21" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
